From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 10:35:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] lsusb: do not warn when the udev hwdb is unavailable

names_init() fails when the udev hwdb is not installed. The 8dev-basic image
intentionally omits udev-hwdb (a large vendor-name database that is dead weight
on fixed hardware), so USB IDs are shown as numbers instead of names, which is
fine. lsusb, however, printed "unable to initialize usb spec" to stderr on every
run. Keep calling names_init() so names still resolve on images that do ship the
hwdb, but drop the noisy warning.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [8dev-basic intentionally omits udev-hwdb]

Signed-off-by: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
---
 lsusb.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lsusb.c b/lsusb.c
--- a/lsusb.c
+++ b/lsusb.c
@@ -3939,8 +3939,7 @@
 
 
 	/* by default, print names as well as numbers */
-	if (names_init() < 0)
-		fprintf(stderr, "unable to initialize usb spec");
+	names_init();
 
 	status = 0;
 
